{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Monrovia homes have downspout problems hiding in plain sight. Builder-grade downspouts on newer homes are often undersized. Older homes may have original downspouts that were never adequate. And plenty of homes have downspouts that dump water right next to the foundation.</p>

<p>On Monrovia's clay soil, water that doesn't drain away pools and eventually finds its way into your home. A properly designed downspout system prevents this by moving water far enough away that it can't cause problems.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Good downspout systems have adequate capacity, proper positioning, and effective extensions.</p>

<p>Capacity means enough downspouts, correctly sized for your roof and local rainfall. Positioning means placing them where water naturally collects. Extensions carry water to safe discharge points far from your foundation.</p>
{% endset %}

